## 1. Introduction to Computer Vision

### What is Computer Vision?
Computer Vision (CV) is a field of artificial intelligence that enables machines to interpret and understand visual information from the world — images, videos, and real-time camera feeds. It aims to replicate and surpass human visual perception by extracting meaningful information from pixel data.

### How Does It Relate to ML/DL?
- **Traditional CV** (pre-2012): Hand-crafted features (SIFT, HOG, SURF) + classical ML classifiers (SVM, Random Forest).
- **Deep Learning CV** (post-2012): End-to-end learning from raw pixels using Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs). Features are learned automatically.
- **Modern CV** (2020+): Transformers (Vision Transformers — ViT), foundation models, multimodal models (CLIP, GPT-4V), diffusion models.

### Key Applications
| Domain | Applications |
|--------|-------------|
| **Healthcare** | Medical image analysis (X-ray, MRI, CT), tumor detection, retinal disease diagnosis |
| **Autonomous Driving** | Lane detection, object detection, pedestrian tracking, sign recognition |
| **Retail** | Visual search, shelf analytics, cashier-less checkout (Amazon Go) |
| **Security** | Surveillance, face recognition, anomaly detection |
| **Manufacturing** | Defect detection, quality inspection, robotic guidance |
| **Agriculture** | Crop disease detection, yield estimation, drone-based monitoring |
| **Entertainment** | AR/VR, deepfakes, image/video generation, style transfer |
| **Document Processing** | OCR, handwriting recognition, document layout analysis |

### Core CV Tasks
| Task | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Image Classification** | Assign a label to an entire image (cat vs dog) |
| **Object Detection** | Locate and classify multiple objects with bounding boxes |
| **Semantic Segmentation** | Classify every pixel into a category |
| **Instance Segmentation** | Like semantic segmentation but distinguishes individual object instances |
| **Panoptic Segmentation** | Combines semantic + instance segmentation |
| **Pose Estimation** | Detect body keypoints (joints, limbs) |
| **Image Generation** | Create new images (GANs, Diffusion Models, VAEs) |
| **Image Super-Resolution** | Upscale low-resolution images |
| **Depth Estimation** | Predict distance of each pixel from the camera |
| **Optical Flow** | Estimate motion between consecutive frames |
| **3D Reconstruction** | Build 3D models from 2D images |
| **Visual Question Answering** | Answer questions about an image |
| **Image Captioning** | Generate text description of an image |

