## 7. Image Classification — Deep Dive

### 7.1 The Task
Given an image, assign it to one (or more) predefined categories.

### 7.2 Key Datasets
| Dataset | Classes | Images | Image Size | Description |
|---------|---------|--------|------------|-------------|
| **MNIST** | 10 | 70K | 28×28 gray | Handwritten digits (0-9) |
| **CIFAR-10** | 10 | 60K | 32×32 color | Tiny natural images |
| **CIFAR-100** | 100 | 60K | 32×32 color | Fine-grained CIFAR |
| **ImageNet (ILSVRC)** | 1,000 | 1.2M | ~256×256 | THE benchmark for classification |
| **Fashion-MNIST** | 10 | 70K | 28×28 gray | Clothing items |
| **Stanford Cars** | 196 | 16K | Variable | Car model recognition |
| **CUB-200** | 200 | 12K | Variable | Bird species |
| **Food-101** | 101 | 101K | Variable | Food classes |

### 7.3 Training Pipeline

```python
import torch
import torchvision.transforms as T
from torchvision import models
from torch.utils.data import DataLoader

# 1. Data Augmentation & Preprocessing
train_transform = T.Compose([
    T.RandomResizedCrop(224),
    T.RandomHorizontalFlip(),
    T.ColorJitter(brightness=0.2, contrast=0.2, saturation=0.2),
    T.ToTensor(),
    T.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406],   # ImageNet mean
                std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225])      # ImageNet std
])

val_transform = T.Compose([
    T.Resize(256),
    T.CenterCrop(224),
    T.ToTensor(),
    T.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225])
])

# 2. Data Loaders
train_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=True, num_workers=4)
val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=False, num_workers=4)

# 3. Model (Transfer Learning)
model = models.resnet50(pretrained=True)
model.fc = torch.nn.Linear(2048, num_classes)  # Replace final layer

# 4. Loss & Optimizer
criterion = torch.nn.CrossEntropyLoss()
optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=1e-4)
scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=epochs)

# 5. Training Loop
for epoch in range(epochs):
    model.train()
    for images, labels in train_loader:
        outputs = model(images)
        loss = criterion(outputs, labels)
        optimizer.zero_grad()
        loss.backward()
        optimizer.step()
    scheduler.step()
```

### 7.4 Loss Functions for Classification
| Loss | Use Case | Formula |
|------|----------|---------|
| **Cross-Entropy** | Multi-class (single label) | $L = -\sum_{c} y_c \log(\hat{y}_c)$ |
| **Binary Cross-Entropy** | Binary or multi-label | $L = -[y\log(\hat{y}) + (1-y)\log(1-\hat{y})]$ |
| **Focal Loss** | Class imbalance | $L = -\alpha(1-\hat{y})^\gamma \log(\hat{y})$ |
| **Label Smoothing CE** | Prevent overconfidence | Uses soft labels: $y_{smooth} = (1-\epsilon)y + \epsilon/K$ |

### 7.5 Evaluation Metrics
| Metric | Formula | Use Case |
|--------|---------|----------|
| **Accuracy** | Correct / Total | Balanced classes |
| **Top-5 Accuracy** | Correct class in top 5 predictions | ImageNet |
| **Precision** | TP / (TP + FP) | When false positives are costly |
| **Recall** | TP / (TP + FN) | When false negatives are costly |
| **F1 Score** | 2 × (P × R) / (P + R) | Balanced precision/recall |
| **Confusion Matrix** | NxN matrix of predictions vs true labels | Per-class analysis |
| **AUC-ROC** | Area under ROC curve | Binary classification |

### 7.6 Transfer Learning & Fine-Tuning

**Transfer Learning** = Using a model pre-trained on a large dataset (ImageNet) as a starting point for a new task.

**Approaches:**
1. **Feature Extraction**: Freeze all pre-trained layers, train only the new classification head.
2. **Fine-Tuning**: Unfreeze some/all pre-trained layers and train with a lower learning rate.
3. **Gradual Unfreezing**: Start with frozen layers; unfreeze layers one at a time from top to bottom.

**When to use which:**
| Your Dataset | Similarity to ImageNet | Strategy |
|-------------|------------------------|----------|
| Small, similar | High | Feature extraction (freeze all) |
| Small, different | Low | Feature extraction + fine-tune top layers |
| Large, similar | High | Fine-tune all with low LR |
| Large, different | Low | Fine-tune all or train from scratch |

```python
# Freeze all layers
for param in model.parameters():
    param.requires_grad = False

# Unfreeze last few layers
for param in model.layer4.parameters():
    param.requires_grad = True

# Different learning rates
optimizer = torch.optim.Adam([
    {'params': model.layer4.parameters(), 'lr': 1e-4},
    {'params': model.fc.parameters(), 'lr': 1e-3}
])
```

